Subject: [PATCH] cppgc: keep table-based GC metadata on Solaris

The Solaris compatibility build sets is_linux for shared build rules. Do not
let that enable the new Linux/macOS object-section GCInfo implementation:
GCC reports section type conflicts for its local and COMDAT instantiations.
Keep the existing GCInfo table fallback; garbage collection stays enabled.

--- a/v8-152.2.0/v8/gni/v8.gni
+++ b/v8-152.2.0/v8/gni/v8.gni
@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@
   cppgc_enable_pointer_compression = false
 
   cppgc_enable_object_section_gcinfo =
-      (is_linux || is_mac) && !is_component_build
+      (is_linux || is_mac) && !is_component_build && target_os != "solaris"
 
   # Enable support for larger cages, up to 16GB.
   # iOS cannot mmap above 8GB, so use the smaller cage.
